---
import type {GetStaticPaths,InferGetStaticPropsType} from 'astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Byline from '../../../components/Byline.astro';
import {getPublishedPieces} from '../../../lib/lab';
import {FARM_SLUG,FARM_PATH,FARM_DESK_PATH,FARM_BLUEPRINT_PATH,FARM_BRIEF_PATH} from '../../../lib/autonomous-farm';
import {farmChapters,farmReferences,observationExample,commandExample} from '../../../lib/farm-blueprint';
import '../../../styles/farm.css';
export const getStaticPaths=(async()=>(await getPublishedPieces()).filter(p=>p.data.slug===FARM_SLUG).map(piece=>({params:{slug:piece.data.slug},props:{piece}}))) satisfies GetStaticPaths;
type Props=InferGetStaticPropsType<typeof getStaticPaths>;
const {piece}=Astro.props;
---
<SiteLayout title="Autonomous farm: technical blueprint | Fidret Lab" description="A detailed cloud-first mixed-farm architecture: observations, water, crops, animals, food lineage, agents, commands, independent protection, sovereignty and evaluation." canonical={`https://fidret.com${FARM_BLUEPRINT_PATH}`} variant="lab">
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="farm-page shell"><header class="farm-page-heading"><a class="text-link" href={FARM_PATH}>The simple explanation</a><h1>Under the farm’s surface.</h1><p class="farm-lead">The advanced blueprint: what each boundary needs to know, enforce and recover before broad automation deserves trust.</p><p>By <Byline authors={piece.data.authors} /> · Researched 4 November 2026 · Fictional architecture, with AI-assisted research and implementation.</p><nav class="farm-reading-routes" aria-label="Farm Lab reading routes"><a href={FARM_DESK_PATH}>Try the scenario desk</a><a href={FARM_BRIEF_PATH} download="fidret-autonomous-farm-brief.md">Download the operating brief</a><a href="#research">Inspect the primary sources</a></nav><p class="farm-scope">A proposed design and teaching model. No real farm, animal, robot, cloud account or personal data is connected. This is not a validated digital twin, operating prescription, certification or legal assessment. Its complexity exposes questions; it does not establish completeness.</p></header>
<div class="farm-blueprint-grid"><aside class="farm-blueprint-index"><nav aria-label="Blueprint sections"><p>Find a boundary</p><ol>{farmChapters.map(c=><li><a href={`#${c.id}`}>{c.title}</a></li>)}<li><a href="#contracts">Example event and command</a></li><li><a href="#research">Research and limits</a></li></ol></nav></aside><div class="farm-blueprint-body">
<section class="farm-architecture-chain" aria-labelledby="farm-chain-title"><h2 id="farm-chain-title">From observation to verified effect</h2><ol><li><strong>Observe</strong> Sensors, machinery and competent local inspection.</li><li><strong>Admit and estimate</strong> Identity, units, quality, age, history and state.</li><li><strong>Propose</strong> Specialist agents explain a bounded plan and uncertainty.</li><li><strong>Check and reserve</strong> Independent policy, shared resources and exact approval.</li><li><strong>Execute locally</strong> Current grant, interlocks, durable command journal.</li><li><strong>Verify and reconcile</strong> Physical evidence, unknown outcomes, farmer response.</li></ol><p>Protection and essential care run alongside this chain. They do not wait for it.</p></section>
{farmChapters.map(c=><section class="farm-chapter" id={c.id} aria-labelledby={`chapter-${c.id}`}><h2 id={`chapter-${c.id}`}>{c.title}</h2><p class="farm-chapter-plain">{c.plain}</p>{c.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}<details><summary>Rehearse this boundary</summary><ul>{c.checks.map(check=><li>{check}</li>)}</ul><p>Proposed tests for a future implementation. These physical/distributed-system rehearsals have not been performed by this Lab.</p></details><p class="farm-source-links">Source basis: {c.sources.map((ref,index)=>{const source=farmReferences.find(r=>r.id===ref)!;return <>{index>0?' · ':''}<a href={`#source-${ref}`}>{source.label}</a></>;})}</p><div class="farm-chapter-return"><a href={FARM_PATH}>Simple version</a><a href={FARM_DESK_PATH}>Explore a situation</a><a href="#main">Section index</a></div></section>)}
<section class="farm-chapter" id="contracts" aria-labelledby="contracts-title"><h2 id="contracts-title">Example event and command</h2><p>Illustrative contract fields, with values deliberately omitted. These are not executable messages or a production schema. Implementations also need versioning, validation, authenticity, retention, bounded cardinality and a reviewed migration contract.</p><h3>An observation envelope</h3><pre><code>{observationExample}</code></pre><h3>A bounded physical command</h3><pre><code>{commandExample}</code></pre><p>The command service and edge must enforce these fields. Describing a limit inside a prompt does not enforce it. The journal protocol must also define crash recovery around physical action.</p></section>
<section class="farm-chapter" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title"><h2 id="research-title">Research and limits</h2><p>The architecture, priority model and scenario combinations are Fidret’s original synthesis. These primary sources support individual domain constraints. They do not validate the combined farm, establish universal thresholds or confirm a Fidret implementation. Living guidance can change. Jurisdiction-specific sources are examples with their scope identified below.</p><p>The Lab models action gating, not crop growth, nutrient chemistry, disease, welfare outcomes, economics, network execution or robot dynamics. It cannot show every possible failure. Simultaneous incidents can require protection, notification and reconciliation together even though a teaching case has one primary answer.</p><div class="farm-references">{farmReferences.map(r=><section id={`source-${r.id}`} aria-labelledby={`source-title-${r.id}`}><h3 id={`source-title-${r.id}`}><a href={r.url}>{r.label}</a></h3><p>{r.scope}</p></section>)}</div><p><a class="text-link" href={`${FARM_PATH}sources/`}>Publication record and article resources</a></p></section>
<section class="farm-next"><h2>Start smaller than this blueprint.</h2><p>Choose one software-only workflow, document the baseline and rehearse its failures. Any physical trial needs qualified people, independent protection, a responsible operator and separate authorization.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={FARM_BRIEF_PATH} download="fidret-autonomous-farm-brief.md">Take the operating brief</a><a class="text-link" href={FARM_PATH}>Return to the simple explanation</a></div></section>
</div></div></main>
</SiteLayout>
